# Playwright and Browser Interaction Rules

## Core Directive
- NEVER launch external browser windows or allow MCP tools to open a visible GUI.
- ALWAYS use the native, built-in Cursor "Integrated Browser Tab" for active web navigation, visual debugging, DOM checking, and element selection.
- All Playwright MCP automated tasks must be executed strictly with the `--headless` flag in the background.

## Workspace Layout
- The user will keep an integrated browser panel open side-by-side on the right side of the workspace.
- When inspecting layouts, checking elements, or debugging failing tests, read from this active view or ask the user to navigate within it if necessary.

## Writing Playwright Test Scripts
- Write clean, modern Playwright locators (e.g., `page.getByRole()`, `page.getByText()`, `page.getByTestId()`).
- Base your element selectors on the accessibility tree and DOM structure exposed via the active in-editor integrated browser.
- If you need to verify a selector or layout, run the headless background tool silently, or use the interactive browser panel. Do not spin up separate headed Chromium processes.

